      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Report finds Kirstie Donnelly and Abid Ismail paid bonuses ‘without authorisation or knowledge’ of superiors </p><p>The two most senior executives at City &amp; Guilds awarded themselves millions of pounds of bonuses “without authorisation from, or knowledge of” their superiors, an internal investigation into last year’s £166m sale of the vocational charity has found.</p><p>The report on the conduct of Kirstie Donnelly, the former chief executive of City &amp; Guilds, and the body’s finance chief, Abid Ismail, sets out how the pair “directly authorised and paid bonuses to themselves” of nearly £3m combined.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jun/15/bosses-city-guilds-millions-bonuses-investigation-kirstie-donnelly-abid-ismail\">Continue reading...</a>"
